percentiles, median_abs_dev; src/stats/mod.rs sum.
percentiles.rs: src/stats/univariate/percentiles.rs at, median, quartiles and
at_unchecked interpolation; sample.rs percentile ordering.
tukey.rs: src/stats/univariate/outliers/tukey.rs classify, Label and LabeledSample
fences/counts/iteration, exposed as original-order diagnostic records.
bootstrap.rs: src/stats/univariate/sample.rs sequential single-sample bootstrap;
src/stats/univariate/resamples.rs Resamples::new/next; src/stats/bivariate/mod.rs
sequential paired bootstrap; src/stats/bivariate/resamples.rs Resamples::new/next.
regression.rs: src/stats/bivariate/mod.rs Data::new/iter;
src/stats/bivariate/regression.rs Slope::fit; src/stats/mod.rs dot.
estimate.rs: src/stats/mod.rs Distribution::from/confidence_interval;
src/estimate.rs Estimate, ConfidenceInterval, build_estimates;
src/analysis/mod.rs estimates and regression estimate assembly.
random.rs: src/stats/rand_util.rs Rng/new_rng and resample index selection.
The multiply-high index algorithm follows oorandom 11.1.5 Rand64::rand_range;
the dependency's MIT attribution accompanies its separately linked license.

Safety adaptations: f64-only validated slice views replace representation casts;
checked counts and finite intermediates replace assertions and unchecked access;
fallible buffers replace unchecked allocation; in-place heapsort and loop
checkpoints make ordinary analysis cooperative. Counts convert exactly within
the documented domains. A sampler-owned recorded seed replaces clock-seeded
thread-local state. Uniform multiply-high rejection checks cancellation on every
attempt and returns a typed error after 128 rejections. No rejected sample becomes
an estimate. All original rows, including Tukey outliers, remain in estimation.
Estimator revision: criterion-0.8.2-nrz-safe-1. Variance uses n-1, scaled MAD uses
1.4826, confidence uses interpolated percentiles, and bootstrap standard error
is the bootstrap sample standard deviation. Successful statistical definitions
are unchanged. A seed reproduces fixed-row statistics, not live timings.

Omitted: two-sample bootstrap (the supplied univariate/mod.rs is provenance
context only), generic float/tuple machinery, r_squared, p values, tails,
relative comparisons, KDE, mixed distributions, parallel execution, clocks,
harnesses, plots, baseline/file/console plumbing and collection/scheduling.
The independent NRZ tests are original additions, not imported upstream tests.

